          "title": "Section 2: Riverside Wildlife Sanctuary Tour Guide",
          "transcript": "Welcome everyone to the Riverside Wildlife Sanctuary. My name is Mark, and I am the head ranger here. Before we set off on the walking trail, I'd like to share some key information about our conservation programmes. The sanctuary was established in 1985 on seventy hectares of protected wetland. We host over one hundred and twenty species of migratory waterbirds. The north hide is the best vantage point for observing kingfishers, particularly in early morning hours. Visitors are reminded that dogs are strictly forbidden on the boardwalk paths to prevent disturbing nesting areas. A cafe serving organic snacks is located next to the main gift shop, open until 5 pm daily.",
