          "title": "Section 3: Academic Tutorial on Marine Ecology Project",
          "transcript": "Tutor: Good afternoon, Emma and Jack. Let's discuss your draft research proposal on urban coral reef restoration. Emma: Thank you, Dr. Harris. We decided to focus our field experiments on artificial reef substrates made from recycled mineral geopolymers. Jack: Exactly. Traditional concrete substrates often leach alkaline chemicals that inhibit coral larval settlement. Geopolymer blocks provide a neutral pH surface. Tutor: That is a well-founded hypothesis. Have you finalized your sampling methodology? Emma: We plan to measure calcification rates over a six-month duration using underwater photogrammetry. Tutor: Excellent. Make sure to account for seasonal variations in water temperature, as summer heatwaves can induce bleaching and skew your baseline growth measurements.",
